rtiallycorrectfeedback><incorrectfeedback format="html"><text /></incorrectfeedback><answer fraction="100.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Personification makes the fence seem to speak softly, creating a quiet, secretive mood.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;A noisy mood because fences are loud.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;A comic mood because fences talk.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;A proud mood because the fence stands tall.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer></question><question type="multichoice"><name><text>CW_U04_L01_R_Q03</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Poem: The road was a ribbon of dust. Which answer best explains the metaphor?&lt;/p&gt;</text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text /></generalfeedback><defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade><penalty>0.3333333</penalty><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answernumbering>none</answernumbering><showstandardinstruction>1</showstandardinstruction><correctfeedback format="html"><text /></correctfeedback><partiallycorrectfeedback format="html"><text /></partiallycorrectfeedback><incorrectfeedback format="html"><text /></incorrectfeedback><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;It creates an angry mood because ribbons are red.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="100.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;The metaphor compares the road to a ribbon, emphasizing its long, narrow shape through the dusty landscape.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;It creates a musical mood because ribbons make sound.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;It creates a crowded mood because roads have cars.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer></question><question type="multichoice"><name><text>CW_U04_L01_R_Q04</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Poem: Stars pricked holes in the black cloth of night. Which mood is strongest?&lt;/p&gt;</text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text /></generalfeedback><defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade><penalty>0.3333333</penalty><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answernumbering>none</answernumbering><showstandardinstruction>1</showstandardinstruction><correctfeedback format="html"><text /></correctfeedback><partiallycorrectfeedback format="html"><text /></partiallycorrectfeedback><incorrectfeedback format="html"><text /></incorrectfeedback><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Silly, because cloth is used for clothes.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Furious, because holes are always violent.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Bored, because stars are common.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="100.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;The metaphorical image makes the night feel vast and mysterious while the stars appear sharp and bright.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer></question><question type="multichoice"><name><text>CW_U04_L01_R_Q05</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Poem: The classroom buzzed like a hive before the bell. What mood does the simile create?&lt;/p&gt;</text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text /></generalfeedback><defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade><penalty>0.3333333</penalty><single>tru